{"author":{"id":"ad87ffa09351c4e5a412ec8ee1546e86b314f33d6f28629bb4bcfe7b2290924d"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794652741,"nonce":"7axjF0AmQ8ewr905z72/6y6Gj/M=","title":"Let a pull request edit its own D1 migrations in place","message":"A preview (pr-N) applies a PR's D1 migrations as they're pushed, and wrangler records only their names in d1_migrations, so editing a migration the PR added leaves the preview's database on the old version, silently. Today the way around it is a new migration, or a new PR (#74 was closed for #76's fresh preview for this reason). Options: record each applied migration's checksum (as the user Durable Object's migration_log does) and, in deploy-preview, recreate the preview's D1 when a migration not on main has changed; or always recreate the preview D1 when the PR's migrations differ from what it applied; or have a check that fails when a migration on main is edited, and let PR-only ones be edited with a reset. Production and staging should still refuse an edited migration.","files":null}]}